From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: ipq5018: scale the CPU between 864 and 1296 MHz

With the PLL change parked on GPLL0 (0973), the CPU can move between
operating points. All three come from the PLL (L = 36, 42, 54 of the
24 MHz XO): the mux driver puts the CPU back on the PLL after every
rate change, so an operating point served by GPLL0, such as the 800 MHz
one 0912 removed, would leave the clock framework and the hardware
disagreeing.

1296 MHz is above the 1008 MHz the SoC is rated for, at the same
1.1 V: the boards have no CPU regulator, so the voltage never changes.
The cpu-thermal passive trip at 100 C already throttles through
cpufreq.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
@@ -95,11 +95,23 @@
 		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
 		opp-shared;
 
+		opp-864000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <864000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <1100000>;
+			clock-latency-ns = <200000>;
+		};
+
 		opp-1008000000 {
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1008000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <1100000>;
 			clock-latency-ns = <200000>;
 		};
+
+		opp-1296000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1296000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <1100000>;
+			clock-latency-ns = <200000>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	firmware {
